Chemical analysis of powders is carried out for quantitative and qualitative information. This is a complicated process with difficulties that can arise in the selection of the appropriate instrument and the correct interpretation of the results. The chart in Figure 1.16 can be used for the selection of the appropriate analytical technique. Atomic absorption spectroscopy (AAS), atomic emission spectrometry (AES) and inductively coupled
