o 10 2 g/cm2s. The evaporators usually used contain a water cooled copper crucible, which collects the evaporated material in the form of an ingot (cast or compacted) with diameter ranging from 25 to 70 mm. The level of the liquid pool surface from which evaporation proceeds is kept constant in most cases, using the mechanism of
